{"step_index":592,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T21:10:22Z","content":"# 🎯 Complete Fix: Problem-Specific Signatures, Testcases & Exact LeetCode Links\n\nThank you for pointing this out — you were spot on! Previously, generic template parameters and Two-Sum test cases were being applied across all problems, and canonical LeetCode slugs had counter suffixes appended.\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ What Has Been Fixed\n\n### 1. Correct Problem-Specific Method Signatures\nEach problem now generates the exact signature required for its input and return types:\n\n#### 🔹 For **Contains Duplicate** (LeetCode 217):\n- **Java**:\n  ```java\n  import java.util.*;\n\n  public class Solution {\n      public boolean solve(int[] nums) {\n          // Write your logic here\n          return false;\n      }\n  }\n  ```\n- **Python 3**:\n  ```python\n  class Solution:\n      def solve(self, nums: list[int]) -> bool:\n          # Write your logic here\n          pass\n  ```\n- **C++**: `bool solve(vector<int>& nums)`\n- **JavaScript**: `function solve(nums)`\n\n#### 🔹 For **Two Sum** (LeetCode 1):\n- **Java**: `public int[] solve(int[] nums, int target)`\n- **Python 3**: `def solve(self, nums: list[int], target: int) -> list[int]:`\n\n#### 🔹 For **Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock** (LeetCode 121):\n- **Java**: `public int solve(int[] prices)`\n- **Python 3**: `def solve(self, prices: list[int]) -> int:`\n\n#### 🔹 For **Climbing Stairs** (LeetCode 70):\n- **Java**: `public int solve(int n)`\n- **Python 3**: `def solve(self, n: int) -> int:`\n\n---\n\n### 2. Matched Problem-Specific Test Cases\n\n#### 🔹 For **Contains Duplicate**:\n| Test Case | Standard Input | Expected Output |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Case 1 (Public)** | `4`<br>`1 2 3 1` | `true` |\n| **Case 2 (Public)** | `4`<br>`1 2 3 4` | `false` |\n| **Case 3 (Hidden)** | `10`<br>`1 1 1 3 3 4 3 2 4 2` | `true` |\n\n#### 🔹 For **Two Sum**:\n| Test Case | Standard Input | Expected Output |\n|---|---